1
00:00:51,691 --> 00:00:55,109
[Episode 2. The Devil's Whisper]

2
00:01:02,127 --> 00:01:04,921
I heard you're friends with Lee Eun Chae.

3
00:01:04,921 --> 00:01:06,881
Give her a message for me.

4
00:01:06,881 --> 00:01:08,327
I'm going to...

5
00:01:08,327 --> 00:01:11,025
sue Seo Jin Woo.

6
00:01:11,761 --> 00:01:13,221
Petty!

7
00:01:18,643 --> 00:01:23,314
You're so petty.

8
00:01:26,854 --> 00:01:30,069
That's rich, coming from you.

9
00:01:31,489 --> 00:01:34,909
If Lee Eun Chae wants to talk to me,

10
00:01:34,909 --> 00:01:38,414
tell her to call me. She has my card.

11
00:01:38,899 --> 00:01:40,737
Pass that on, please.

12
00:01:49,966 --> 00:01:51,709
Ugh, seriously.

13
00:01:56,181 --> 00:01:57,628
[Seo Jin Woo]
Yes?

14
00:02:02,896 --> 00:02:04,360
Eun Chae.

15
00:02:19,268 --> 00:02:21,098
Eun Chae, what's wrong?

16
00:02:23,583 --> 00:02:25,919
Nothing's wrong, exactly.

17
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,291
It's more that I did something...

18
00:02:32,119 --> 00:02:33,712
What happened?

19
00:02:34,855 --> 00:02:36,721
Jin Woo...

20
00:02:42,729 --> 00:02:46,033
Jin Woo,
do you have a patient named Kwon Do Hyeok?

21
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:49,221
I pretended to be a doctor in front of him.

22
00:02:49,221 --> 00:02:51,056
I'm so sorry.

23
00:02:51,884 --> 00:02:55,580
Now he says he's suing you and the hospital.

24
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:58,785
He told me he's a sex addict.

25
00:02:58,785 --> 00:02:59,911
I think that's why.

26
00:02:59,911 --> 00:03:02,089
I'm so sorry, really.

27
00:03:04,999 --> 00:03:08,816
Do Hyeok said he's a sex addict?

28
00:03:12,006 --> 00:03:15,051
Looks like Do Hyeok fooled you too.

29
00:03:15,051 --> 00:03:17,313
Kwon Do Hyeok is my friend.

30
00:03:18,232 --> 00:03:20,434
Jin Woo.

31
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:22,433
Why are you friends with that guy?

32
00:03:22,433 --> 00:03:24,060
I'll call him.

33
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,120
Don't worry, Eun Chae.

34
00:03:29,232 --> 00:03:30,859
It's me.

35
00:03:30,859 --> 00:03:32,193
<i>What's up?</i>

36
00:03:32,193 --> 00:03:35,405
I need to see you. Can you make time?

37
00:03:35,405 --> 00:03:37,240
Not sure.

38
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,950
<i>We need to meet today.</i>

39
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:41,333
You wanted to meet Eun Chae.

40
00:03:43,997 --> 00:03:45,832
Did she confess?

41
00:03:45,832 --> 00:03:50,420
<i>You two have some things to talk out,
so make some time.</i>

42
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:53,172
Or I'm done being your doctor.

43
00:03:53,172 --> 00:03:56,634
Wow, you're coming on strong, Seo Jin Woo.

44
00:03:56,634 --> 00:03:58,799
It's about my sister-in-law.

45
00:03:59,651 --> 00:04:02,390
I can't stop you from tormenting other people,

46
00:04:02,390 --> 00:04:05,435
but mess with my sister-in-law,
I won't sit still.

47
00:04:05,435 --> 00:04:06,975
Jin Woo.

48
00:04:19,908 --> 00:04:21,409
You...

49
00:04:21,409 --> 00:04:23,870
There can only be one of you.

50
00:04:29,313 --> 00:04:32,170
I think you two have a misunderstanding,

51
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:35,214
so talk it out over drinks.

52
00:04:35,214 --> 00:04:37,342
There's no misunderstanding.

53
00:04:37,342 --> 00:04:40,433
Fact is,
your sister-in-law impersonated a doctor.

54
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:44,724
Be careful.

55
00:04:44,724 --> 00:04:47,727
When I get drunk, I hit people I don't like.

56
00:04:47,727 --> 00:04:50,474
Hit me,
and your family will pay for generations.

57
00:04:52,273 --> 00:04:54,734
I didn't invite Do Hyeok here to fight.

58
00:04:54,734 --> 00:04:57,904
You were wrong to pose as a doctor.

59
00:04:57,904 --> 00:05:00,544
Any other patient would've been genuinely hurt.

60
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:06,496
So you mean I'm heartless,
and nothing hurts me?

61
00:05:06,496 --> 00:05:11,066
<i>Some "hurt" guy he is,
going around threatening to sue.</i>

62
00:05:12,585 --> 00:05:14,337
If you apologize first,

63
00:05:14,337 --> 00:05:16,577
Do Hyeok won't make a fuss anymore.

64
00:05:24,334 --> 00:05:26,182
Then put it in writing.

65
00:05:26,182 --> 00:05:27,767
I can't just take his word.

66
00:05:27,767 --> 00:05:29,769
Fine. I'll write it.

67
00:05:29,769 --> 00:05:31,562
It's just a pledge.

68
00:05:31,562 --> 00:05:32,814
Really?

69
00:05:32,814 --> 00:05:34,649
You'll write a pledge?

70
00:05:34,649 --> 00:05:37,485
So all this time, my so-called friend,

71
00:05:37,485 --> 00:05:39,556
what did you take me for?

72
00:05:43,574 --> 00:05:46,077
I need to take this call.

73
00:05:46,077 --> 00:05:48,329
Work it out and write it up.

74
00:05:48,329 --> 00:05:49,539
Don't fight.

75
00:05:49,539 --> 00:05:51,541
What kind of person... Answer me.

76
00:05:51,541 --> 00:05:53,075
Hello?

77
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:05,096
Isn't Jin Woo your sister's husband?

78
00:06:05,096 --> 00:06:08,184
You look like a duckling that lost its mother.

79
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:11,614
You don't have to talk like that.

80
00:06:13,073 --> 00:06:15,077
That friend of yours, Soo,

81
00:06:15,077 --> 00:06:18,415
is better than you at passing
on messages right away.

82
00:06:18,415 --> 00:06:20,313
Why would you tell Soo that?

83
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,530
Because you won't answer my calls!

84
00:06:22,530 --> 00:06:23,963
Calls?

85
00:06:25,349 --> 00:06:27,041
[Blocked]

86
00:06:33,093 --> 00:06:34,372
No way...

87
00:06:35,293 --> 00:06:36,681
You blocked me?

88
00:06:49,676 --> 00:06:55,276
<i>The person you're calling is unavailable.
Please try again...</i>

89
00:06:57,774 --> 00:06:59,935
How dare you block me?

90
00:07:02,737 --> 00:07:06,240
That means you haven't seen any texts I sent!

91
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,617
I'll unblock you.

92
00:07:07,617 --> 00:07:09,798
Unblocking now.

93
00:07:11,871 --> 00:07:13,337
Done.

94
00:07:15,374 --> 00:07:18,799
Now that it's unblocked,
let's write that pledge.

95
00:07:21,339 --> 00:07:22,840
Forget the pledge.

96
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:25,384
How about a contract instead?

97
00:07:25,384 --> 00:07:27,915
You don't feel like apologizing anyway.

98
00:07:27,915 --> 00:07:29,799
<i>He's a mind reader.</i>

99
00:07:32,016 --> 00:07:34,602
What kind of contract?

100
00:07:34,602 --> 00:07:36,395
Three months, starting now.

101
00:07:36,395 --> 00:07:38,022
Come work as my secretary.

102
00:07:38,022 --> 00:07:40,358
Secretary? Why would I work for you?

103
00:07:40,358 --> 00:07:45,516
Isn't it better than working
at Taeyun Home Shopping's call center?

104
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:48,658
You're quite the habitual liar.

105
00:07:48,658 --> 00:07:53,052
<i>What's pathetic is
that I got fired from there too.</i>

106
00:07:56,374 --> 00:07:57,510
No way...

107
00:07:57,510 --> 00:08:00,753
You didn't tell Jin Woo, did you?

108
00:08:00,753 --> 00:08:02,141
I will if you don't.

109
00:08:02,141 --> 00:08:04,553
What a petty man!

110
00:08:05,883 --> 00:08:07,468
<i>Wait.</i>

111
00:08:07,468 --> 00:08:09,846
<i>This is actually a good deal for me.</i>

112
00:08:09,846 --> 00:08:12,492
<i>Why on earth though?</i>

113
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:17,228
Are you doing this to me because of Soo?

114
00:08:18,298 --> 00:08:20,189
Smarter than I expected.

115
00:08:20,189 --> 00:08:21,482
What if I am?

116
00:08:21,482 --> 00:08:23,818
Why are you so obsessed with Soo?

117
00:08:23,818 --> 00:08:27,273
When a man wants to see a woman,
there's only one reason.

118
00:08:27,273 --> 00:08:31,878
Sorry,
but Soo won't be attracted to you one bit.

119
00:08:31,878 --> 00:08:33,327
I doubt that.

120
00:08:33,327 --> 00:08:35,225
<i>What do you mean, you doubt that?</i>

121
00:08:35,225 --> 00:08:37,947
<i>If I say so, then it's so.</i>

122
00:08:37,947 --> 00:08:41,169
Women who said that ended up falling for me.

123
00:08:42,086 --> 00:08:45,089
<i>He actually means it.</i>

124
00:08:45,089 --> 00:08:49,233
And I'm sure you'll fall for me too.

125
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:53,764
Even if you were the only man in the world,

126
00:08:53,764 --> 00:08:55,084
I wouldn't want you.

127
00:08:55,084 --> 00:08:56,475
That'll never happen.

128
00:08:56,475 --> 00:08:58,874
Don't get so full of yourself.

129
00:09:00,313 --> 00:09:03,191
If you stick to that till the end,

130
00:09:03,191 --> 00:09:04,978
then I'll apologize.

131
00:09:04,978 --> 00:09:09,947
<i>He'd get on his knees and apologize to me?</i>

132
00:09:09,947 --> 00:09:13,720
That's the most tempting thing
I've heard all day.

133
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:17,290
Or I could grant you something even bigger.

134
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,792
<i>Oh, really?</i>

135
00:09:18,792 --> 00:09:22,038
<i>Then should I name something bigger?</i>

136
00:09:24,253 --> 00:09:26,214
Then let's make a bet.

137
00:09:26,214 --> 00:09:27,568
Okay, deal.

138
00:09:27,568 --> 00:09:31,036
Whoever wins this bet gets whatever they want.

139
00:09:35,957 --> 00:09:37,934
<i>I just have to last three months.</i>

140
00:09:37,934 --> 00:09:41,020
<i>No way I'll fall for a guy like that.</i>

141
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:43,773
<i>I just have to keep her for three months.</i>

142
00:09:43,773 --> 00:09:47,193
<i>She's bound to fall for me.</i>

143
00:09:47,193 --> 00:09:48,402
Okay, deal.

144
00:09:48,402 --> 00:09:49,791
Then...

145
00:09:50,404 --> 00:09:53,115
before anything else,
let's write the contract now.

146
00:09:53,115 --> 00:09:54,992
Right now?

147
00:09:54,992 --> 00:09:56,285
Okay.

148
00:09:56,285 --> 00:09:58,939
Should I have brought a tablet?

149
00:10:01,115 --> 00:10:04,418
So people still use notebooks these days.

150
00:10:04,418 --> 00:10:05,711
Of course.

151
00:10:12,718 --> 00:10:14,147
By the way,

152
00:10:14,147 --> 00:10:17,867
how much does a secretary get paid?

153
00:10:18,808 --> 00:10:20,587
How much do you want?

154
00:10:20,587 --> 00:10:23,446
Salaries are negotiable, so name your price.

155
00:10:23,446 --> 00:10:25,959
Then ten million won upfront. Or I won't do it.

156
00:10:25,959 --> 00:10:27,275
Fine.

157
00:10:27,275 --> 00:10:32,029
But if you take it first and want to quit,
you can't.

158
00:10:32,029 --> 00:10:33,753
Are you aware?

159
00:10:35,102 --> 00:10:36,794
Okay, deal.

160
00:10:48,254 --> 00:10:49,387
Not taking it?

161
00:10:49,387 --> 00:10:51,684
You just carry million-won checks around?

162
00:10:51,684 --> 00:10:52,717
Yes.

163
00:10:52,717 --> 00:10:55,219
Like the loose change in yours.

164
00:11:08,691 --> 00:11:09,971
Sign.

165
00:11:21,648 --> 00:11:26,375
And you must never
tell anyone about this contract.

166
00:11:26,375 --> 00:11:27,777
Done deal.

167
00:11:33,022 --> 00:11:35,110
Made up while I was gone?

168
00:11:35,829 --> 00:11:38,727
We made up nice and clean.

169
00:11:40,801 --> 00:11:42,676
Okay, then let's have a drink.

170
00:12:23,933 --> 00:12:26,727
Lee Eun Chae! What brings you here?

171
00:12:26,727 --> 00:12:28,813
What?

172
00:12:28,813 --> 00:12:30,941
What are you doing right now?

173
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:55,097
You...

174
00:12:55,097 --> 00:12:57,550
- What is this?
- What's it look like?

175
00:12:57,550 --> 00:13:01,679
I paid the settlement,
so you need to sign the agreement.

176
00:13:01,679 --> 00:13:03,681
Oh, please.

177
00:13:03,681 --> 00:13:04,932
Team Leader Yeo.

178
00:13:04,932 --> 00:13:06,428
- Yes?
- Get to it.

179
00:13:06,428 --> 00:13:07,560
Eun Chae.

180
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,894
Eun Chae, what's this?

181
00:13:08,894 --> 00:13:11,021
Not that.

182
00:13:11,021 --> 00:13:14,400
Check if it's really ten million won.

183
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,235
All of this?

184
00:13:16,235 --> 00:13:18,946
You wait until I count all this.

185
00:13:18,946 --> 00:13:21,182
How many are there?

186
00:13:22,658 --> 00:13:25,842
One, two, three, four, five.

187
00:13:25,842 --> 00:13:30,207
- What are you doing? Count with me!
- This is our office! Don't sit down!

188
00:13:30,207 --> 00:13:32,126
What a nutcase.

189
00:13:33,586 --> 00:13:34,879
Over here!

190
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:37,840
And order me some sushi.

191
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,842
Okay.

192
00:13:52,799 --> 00:13:54,940
<i>Start work on Wednesday.</i>

193
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,777
<i>At the address below.</i>

194
00:13:57,318 --> 00:13:59,109
OYES Entertainment?

195
00:14:00,029 --> 00:14:01,574
No way.

196
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:04,999
Is he actually interested in our music?

197
00:14:09,622 --> 00:14:12,124
A new secretary starts today.

198
00:14:12,124 --> 00:14:13,286
A new one?

199
00:14:13,286 --> 00:14:16,562
I need someone I can hand things off to, too.

200
00:14:17,296 --> 00:14:19,346
So who...

201
00:14:22,676 --> 00:14:23,802
Over there.

202
00:14:23,802 --> 00:14:25,012
There she is.

203
00:14:35,965 --> 00:14:39,276
From now on, my work can be left to Eun Chae.

204
00:14:39,276 --> 00:14:40,486
Yes.

205
00:14:41,695 --> 00:14:43,316
And...

206
00:14:43,316 --> 00:14:46,450
Lee Eun Chae's most important duty is

207
00:14:46,450 --> 00:14:50,906
to respond right away when I call.

208
00:14:53,290 --> 00:14:54,366
Yes.

209
00:15:04,218 --> 00:15:05,469
Secretarial work is

210
00:15:05,469 --> 00:15:09,014
managing the CEO's schedule
and accompanying him.

211
00:15:09,014 --> 00:15:10,558
This will be your desk.

212
00:15:10,558 --> 00:15:13,143
General Affairs will provide supplies.

213
00:15:13,143 --> 00:15:16,564
You'll pick things up as you go.

214
00:15:16,564 --> 00:15:18,524
Yes. Understood.

215
00:15:18,524 --> 00:15:21,652
First, when the CEO arrives,
prepare his coffee.

216
00:15:21,652 --> 00:15:24,833
The coffee can't be too hot or too cold.

217
00:15:27,074 --> 00:15:29,702
<i>Picky guy.</i>

218
00:15:29,702 --> 00:15:34,300
Lunch is at 11:30.
At 6:00, check with the CEO about dinner.

219
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,959
Bring a few menu options when you go in.

220
00:15:36,959 --> 00:15:38,130
However,

221
00:15:38,130 --> 00:15:42,798
when the CEO is in the lab,
never, ever disturb him.

222
00:15:42,798 --> 00:15:44,343
Okay.

223
00:15:46,427 --> 00:15:49,314
Eun Chae, shall we start work?

224
00:15:49,314 --> 00:15:50,349
Yes.

225
00:15:50,349 --> 00:15:52,182
No, I meant the phone.

226
00:15:52,182 --> 00:15:53,475
Oh, yes.

227
00:15:58,137 --> 00:15:59,607
Hel...

228
00:15:59,607 --> 00:16:01,233
Hello?

229
00:16:21,462 --> 00:16:24,657
When that intercom rings, it's me calling,

230
00:16:24,657 --> 00:16:28,177
so skip the "Hel... hello."

231
00:16:30,035 --> 00:16:31,339
Yes.

232
00:16:38,103 --> 00:16:41,357
Five degrees warmer.

233
00:16:41,357 --> 00:16:42,843
Five degrees?

234
00:16:42,843 --> 00:16:45,734
<i>He's pickier than I thought.</i>

235
00:16:55,162 --> 00:16:56,900
Already smitten?

236
00:16:57,972 --> 00:16:59,724
What are you talking about?

237
00:17:20,307 --> 00:17:23,691
I told you very clearly to drop the artist.

238
00:17:23,691 --> 00:17:27,210
Why hasn't it been reported in the press yet?

239
00:17:27,210 --> 00:17:28,247
Well...

240
00:17:28,247 --> 00:17:30,651
I think it needs more discussion.

241
00:17:31,532 --> 00:17:34,832
And Mrs. Jeong opposes it too.

242
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:42,628
The decision-maker here right now is me.

243
00:17:43,293 --> 00:17:45,921
Your unilateral decision...

244
00:17:45,921 --> 00:17:47,756
I can't accept it.

245
00:17:47,756 --> 00:17:50,217
If the problem continues, we'll have to recode.

246
00:17:50,217 --> 00:17:54,012
Not just the artists,
but all of you here as well.

247
00:17:55,389 --> 00:17:58,016
If you don't like that,
bring me an alternative.

248
00:18:07,484 --> 00:18:09,945
Coding? Computers?

249
00:18:09,945 --> 00:18:11,530
What is he, a programmer?

250
00:18:11,530 --> 00:18:13,032
Where did coding come from?

251
00:18:13,032 --> 00:18:16,103
All those computers,
and what is he even researching?

252
00:18:16,963 --> 00:18:19,879
Director Lee, did you report to Mrs. Jeong?

253
00:18:19,879 --> 00:18:21,625
Of course I did.

254
00:18:21,625 --> 00:18:23,041
Don't worry.

255
00:18:23,041 --> 00:18:26,978
Mrs. Jeong is the largest shareholder.
What can he possibly do?

256
00:18:26,978 --> 00:18:28,340
Let's go.

257
00:18:31,108 --> 00:18:34,386
What matters here is character consistency.

258
00:18:34,386 --> 00:18:37,054
<i>How about adding a voice? Hi.</i>

259
00:18:38,056 --> 00:18:39,267
<i>Hi!</i>

260
00:18:41,655 --> 00:18:43,019
<i>Not bad.</i>

261
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:45,397
Hardly.

262
00:18:46,356 --> 00:18:48,160
The voice won't be easy either.

263
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,526
<i>By the way,</i>

264
00:18:49,526 --> 00:18:51,445
<i>what should we call her?</i>

265
00:18:51,445 --> 00:18:53,280
Let's see...

266
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:02,056
A free-spirited girl.

267
00:19:03,499 --> 00:19:04,833
Caroline.

268
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:07,987
Carol.

269
00:19:13,787 --> 00:19:17,860
Why does my first day have to be a Wednesday?

270
00:19:23,519 --> 00:19:24,978
Where's the CEO?

271
00:19:24,978 --> 00:19:27,564
He's still in the lab.

272
00:19:27,564 --> 00:19:29,650
But, Mr. Park,

273
00:19:29,650 --> 00:19:32,778
would it be okay if I left a little early?

274
00:19:32,778 --> 00:19:36,176
I go to English class every Wednesday.

275
00:19:36,176 --> 00:19:39,140
Everything's global these days.

276
00:19:42,985 --> 00:19:45,082
Sure. Go ahead and leave.

277
00:19:45,082 --> 00:19:47,084
I'll tell him when he's out of the lab.

278
00:19:47,084 --> 00:19:48,335
Okay.

279
00:19:48,335 --> 00:19:49,819
Thank you.

280
00:19:53,549 --> 00:19:55,395
Enjoy your din-din!

281
00:19:58,136 --> 00:19:59,510
What's din-din?

282
00:20:14,403 --> 00:20:17,373
- Yes.
<i>- Come in for a second.</i>

283
00:20:17,373 --> 00:20:18,666
Understood.

284
00:20:19,449 --> 00:20:22,703
She has English class on Wednesdays,
so I let her leave.

285
00:20:22,703 --> 00:20:25,770
<i>Wednesday...</i>

286
00:20:25,770 --> 00:20:29,217
Who said you could send her home
without my permission?

287
00:20:31,295 --> 00:20:32,796
I'm sorry.

288
00:20:32,796 --> 00:20:35,924
I didn't want to disturb you
while you were in the lab.

289
00:20:35,924 --> 00:20:38,376
It won't happen again.

290
00:20:41,373 --> 00:20:44,276
Go home as well, Mr. Park.

291
00:20:44,276 --> 00:20:47,514
You've been working late far too often lately.

292
00:20:47,514 --> 00:20:50,108
At this rate, you'll wear yourself out.

293
00:21:08,396 --> 00:21:10,335
[Psychopath]

294
00:21:15,179 --> 00:21:16,465
Hello?

295
00:21:16,465 --> 00:21:18,884
Leaving without my permission

296
00:21:18,884 --> 00:21:20,802
is a breach of contract.

297
00:21:20,802 --> 00:21:23,196
Come on, since when?

298
00:21:23,196 --> 00:21:25,157
It's all in the contract.

299
00:21:28,861 --> 00:21:31,772
I'm in class right now.

300
00:21:31,772 --> 00:21:33,227
I'll call after class.

301
00:21:33,227 --> 00:21:36,860
Do you know the penalty for breach of contract?

302
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:38,487
Penalty?

303
00:21:38,487 --> 00:21:40,559
Get over here right now.

304
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:43,664
You have one hour.

305
00:21:49,122 --> 00:21:53,168
What kind of devil is this guy?

306
00:21:54,635 --> 00:21:58,429
Ugh, seriously.

307
00:22:44,469 --> 00:22:48,640
I decide when to get off work.

308
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:54,340
Leaving without permission
is a serious breach of contract.

309
00:22:55,313 --> 00:22:56,416
What are you saying?

310
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:57,959
You told...

311
00:22:59,505 --> 00:23:01,265
You said you were learning English.

312
00:23:02,529 --> 00:23:04,161
I'm only a beginner.

313
00:23:04,161 --> 00:23:05,574
Never mind that.

314
00:23:05,574 --> 00:23:08,119
So how much is the penalty?

315
00:23:17,252 --> 00:23:19,546
<i>For the next three months, Lee Eun Chae</i>

316
00:23:19,546 --> 00:23:21,840
<i>works as Kwon Do Hyeok's personal secretary.</i>

317
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:24,301
<i>During those three months, her hours</i>

318
00:23:24,301 --> 00:23:27,137
<i>and all duties are set by Kwon Do Hyeok.</i>

319
00:23:27,137 --> 00:23:29,347
<i>Outside employment is prohibited.</i>

320
00:23:29,347 --> 00:23:31,850
<i>If Kwon Do Hyeok gives separate instructions,</i>

321
00:23:31,850 --> 00:23:34,394
<i>she will carry them out.</i>

322
00:23:34,394 --> 00:23:37,481
<i>Details of this contract will not be disclosed.</i>

323
00:23:37,481 --> 00:23:39,358
<i>Sounds right.</i>

324
00:23:39,358 --> 00:23:41,234
<i>After the three-month period ends,</i>

325
00:23:41,234 --> 00:23:42,655
<i>if Kwon Do Hyeok loses the bet,</i>

326
00:23:42,655 --> 00:23:44,946
<i>he must grant Lee Eun Chae's demands,</i>

327
00:23:44,946 --> 00:23:46,448
<i>and if Lee Eun Chae loses,</i>

328
00:23:46,448 --> 00:23:49,127
<i>she must grant Kwon Do Hyeok's demands.</i>

329
00:23:50,035 --> 00:23:52,204
<i>In case of breach of contract,</i>

330
00:23:52,204 --> 00:23:56,448
<i>the penalty is three times the amount received.</i>

331
00:23:57,751 --> 00:23:59,354
Three times?

332
00:24:00,116 --> 00:24:03,249
[30 million won]

333
00:24:06,593 --> 00:24:07,636
<i>What?</i>

334
00:24:07,636 --> 00:24:09,673
<i>Overtime on your first day?</i>

335
00:24:10,305 --> 00:24:13,225
The old me would've quit on the spot.

336
00:24:13,225 --> 00:24:15,143
<i>Why can't you now?</i>

337
00:24:15,143 --> 00:24:16,624
Well,

338
00:24:20,065 --> 00:24:22,901
guess it's time I grew up.

339
00:24:24,444 --> 00:24:27,239
<i>But what about the show?</i>

340
00:24:27,239 --> 00:24:29,825
Come on, it's weird without you.

341
00:24:31,159 --> 00:24:34,204
<i>Eun Chae, will it be like this from now on?</i>

342
00:24:35,163 --> 00:24:36,718
I'm really sorry...

343
00:24:36,718 --> 00:24:38,166
But...

344
00:24:38,166 --> 00:24:40,354
even I don't know what to expect.

345
00:24:43,296 --> 00:24:44,714
The CEO is

346
00:24:44,714 --> 00:24:46,633
<i>a total sociopath.</i>

347
00:24:46,633 --> 00:24:49,136
<i>He has no empathy.</i>

348
00:24:49,136 --> 00:24:50,637
Wait, a sociopath?

349
00:24:50,637 --> 00:24:52,806
Eun Chae, are you okay?

350
00:24:52,806 --> 00:24:53,932
<i>So far.</i>

351
00:24:53,932 --> 00:24:57,018
I just made a deal with the devil.

352
00:24:57,018 --> 00:24:58,518
Hold on.

353
00:24:58,518 --> 00:25:01,356
We can't do our first gig without you, though.

354
00:25:01,356 --> 00:25:02,566
A gig?

355
00:25:02,566 --> 00:25:04,436
We got a gig?

356
00:25:04,436 --> 00:25:06,987
<i>It's this Friday evening.</i>

357
00:25:06,987 --> 00:25:08,238
<i>Tough, right?</i>

358
00:25:08,238 --> 00:25:09,656
No. No, no.

359
00:25:09,656 --> 00:25:10,699
I'll be there!

360
00:25:10,699 --> 00:25:12,318
No matter what.

361
00:25:50,617 --> 00:25:52,908
It's only once a month.

362
00:25:52,908 --> 00:25:55,345
Who said anything?

363
00:25:56,678 --> 00:25:57,971
Here.

364
00:25:59,164 --> 00:26:00,965
Mrs. Jeong likes these.

365
00:26:01,962 --> 00:26:04,375
No need to make an enemy of her.

366
00:26:39,677 --> 00:26:41,837
<i>Mom.</i>

367
00:27:00,559 --> 00:27:02,727
<i>Mom.</i>

368
00:27:43,059 --> 00:27:45,145
Do Hyeok!

369
00:27:45,145 --> 00:27:48,392
What took you so long?

370
00:27:50,025 --> 00:27:51,651
I missed you.

371
00:27:51,651 --> 00:27:53,792
Can't you come home more often?

372
00:28:06,778 --> 00:28:08,258
You're here.

373
00:28:11,365 --> 00:28:12,630
Here.

374
00:28:12,630 --> 00:28:14,625
Oh, my.

375
00:28:15,747 --> 00:28:17,598
Look at this.

376
00:28:17,598 --> 00:28:21,222
I can't remember the last time
a man gave me flowers.

377
00:28:21,222 --> 00:28:23,221
It's only once a month.

378
00:28:24,059 --> 00:28:25,688
Can't you even be on time?

379
00:28:29,731 --> 00:28:31,141
Let's sit.

380
00:28:33,780 --> 00:28:37,576
You could've talked to me
about making Do Hyeok the CEO.

381
00:28:40,988 --> 00:28:43,998
I heard one of the idols got into trouble.
You okay?

382
00:28:45,292 --> 00:28:47,805
You won't really drop him, will you?

383
00:28:48,375 --> 00:28:50,877
You should talk to me about this.

384
00:28:50,877 --> 00:28:53,011
I built that agency, didn't I?

385
00:28:59,427 --> 00:29:01,265
That won't do.

386
00:29:03,223 --> 00:29:06,476
You're new to this, Do Hyeok,
so I suppose you wouldn't know.

387
00:29:06,476 --> 00:29:10,675
We built our agency as a cultural
enterprise rather than for money.

388
00:29:11,439 --> 00:29:12,690
Isn't that so, Chairman?

389
00:29:12,690 --> 00:29:17,200
My father sent me to the agency for results.

390
00:29:17,987 --> 00:29:19,160
But...

391
00:29:20,281 --> 00:29:22,707
there are many risks right now.

392
00:29:24,369 --> 00:29:27,122
If the agency needs any promo, just ask.

393
00:29:27,122 --> 00:29:29,916
I have over a million followers.

394
00:29:29,916 --> 00:29:31,626
Keep your promise.

395
00:29:31,626 --> 00:29:33,790
You asked for three months.

396
00:29:34,857 --> 00:29:36,066
Yes.

397
00:29:57,402 --> 00:29:59,972
<i>It's this Friday evening.</i>

398
00:29:59,972 --> 00:30:01,199
<i>Tough, right?</i>

399
00:30:01,199 --> 00:30:02,668
<i>No. No, no.</i>

400
00:30:02,668 --> 00:30:03,742
<i>I'll be there!</i>

401
00:30:03,742 --> 00:30:05,618
<i>No matter what.</i>

402
00:30:05,618 --> 00:30:07,620
Should I say I'm sick and leave early?

403
00:30:07,620 --> 00:30:10,216
Would he let me? That devil?

404
00:30:12,024 --> 00:30:13,710
No.

405
00:30:13,710 --> 00:30:16,129
I'll just skip work altogether.

406
00:30:20,142 --> 00:30:21,801
Lee Eun Chae.

407
00:30:21,801 --> 00:30:23,344
Good morning.

408
00:30:23,344 --> 00:30:25,054
Yes, good morning!

409
00:30:25,054 --> 00:30:27,745
- Let's go in.
- Yes, after you.

410
00:30:36,579 --> 00:30:38,537
I heard the surgery went well.

411
00:30:38,537 --> 00:30:40,489
That's Moon Tae Gyeong for you.

412
00:30:40,489 --> 00:30:42,113
I hear it was a difficult one.

413
00:30:42,113 --> 00:30:44,286
I'm glad it went well.

414
00:30:45,700 --> 00:30:48,703
Talented and humble? Come on.

415
00:30:48,703 --> 00:30:52,521
No wonder you're first
in the nurses' popularity vote.

416
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,461
There's no such vote, Jin Woo.

417
00:30:56,461 --> 00:30:58,930
Jin Woo, when do you get off?

418
00:30:58,930 --> 00:31:00,988
Want to grab a drink? It's been a while.

419
00:31:00,988 --> 00:31:03,031
Bring Eun Seo, too.

420
00:31:03,031 --> 00:31:06,558
When you get off this early, go on a date, kid.

421
00:31:08,473 --> 00:31:10,315
Too bad, though.

422
00:31:10,315 --> 00:31:12,129
I'm on night duty today.

423
00:31:17,690 --> 00:31:21,123
<i>Jin Woo, you're coming to see
our gig today, right?</i>

424
00:31:24,197 --> 00:31:26,481
Why? Is something wrong?

425
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:30,989
Tae Gyeong, let me ask you a favor.

426
00:31:31,829 --> 00:31:35,166
I just need you to deliver something for me.

427
00:31:35,166 --> 00:31:36,261
Sure.

428
00:31:36,261 --> 00:31:40,421
But keep this a secret from Eun Seo.

429
00:31:40,421 --> 00:31:41,714
Got it?

430
00:31:42,382 --> 00:31:44,403
Okay!

431
00:31:50,807 --> 00:31:53,270
<i>You know the show's at 7:00, right?</i>

432
00:31:56,729 --> 00:31:58,815
What's the schedule today?

433
00:31:58,815 --> 00:32:02,235
We leave now. There's one meeting
before the executive dinner.

434
00:32:02,235 --> 00:32:05,572
Once the dinner is over,
it should be about 8:00.

435
00:32:05,572 --> 00:32:07,699
<i>Aha.</i>

436
00:32:07,699 --> 00:32:09,324
Eun Chae.

437
00:32:13,121 --> 00:32:14,501
Are you heading out?

438
00:32:14,501 --> 00:32:15,794
Yes.

439
00:32:17,041 --> 00:32:18,751
Why?

440
00:32:18,751 --> 00:32:21,108
- Is something up?
- No.

441
00:32:21,108 --> 00:32:24,120
- I was just wondering if you needed anything.
- There is.

442
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:27,197
Sort the OYES Entertainment
articles by algorithm.

443
00:32:27,197 --> 00:32:28,263
By when?

444
00:32:28,263 --> 00:32:29,905
By the time I'm back.

445
00:32:32,307 --> 00:32:33,474
Handle dinner yourself.

446
00:32:33,474 --> 00:32:34,900
Din-din's on you.

447
00:32:36,060 --> 00:32:37,729
Yes, understood.

448
00:32:42,194 --> 00:32:43,818
Wait a second.

449
00:32:43,818 --> 00:32:45,695
The show's at 7:00,

450
00:32:45,695 --> 00:32:48,364
so I can be back around 8:30.

451
00:32:49,574 --> 00:32:52,118
That's worth a shot, right?

452
00:33:02,784 --> 00:33:05,186
<i>I'll be back after dinner!</i>

453
00:33:25,193 --> 00:33:26,819
Are you okay?

454
00:33:26,819 --> 00:33:29,133
I'm fine.

455
00:33:36,996 --> 00:33:39,082
Haven't we met somewhere?

456
00:33:39,082 --> 00:33:42,752
<i>Where does he get his pickup line?</i>

457
00:33:42,752 --> 00:33:44,337
No, we haven't.

458
00:33:45,824 --> 00:33:48,013
Want me to carry that to wherever you're going?

459
00:33:48,944 --> 00:33:51,094
If you like helping people so much,

460
00:33:51,094 --> 00:33:53,357
you should be a social worker.

461
00:33:54,013 --> 00:33:55,390
Yes.

462
00:33:55,390 --> 00:33:57,728
Actually, I do a similar job.

463
00:33:57,728 --> 00:33:59,155
I see.

464
00:34:00,186 --> 00:34:01,854
I'm short on time.

465
00:34:01,854 --> 00:34:03,147
Take care.

466
00:34:09,016 --> 00:34:11,254
I'm headed that way anyway.

467
00:35:18,048 --> 00:35:19,642
Are you okay?

468
00:35:21,382 --> 00:35:24,171
You really should be a social worker.

469
00:35:25,438 --> 00:35:26,513
Sorry?

470
00:35:31,231 --> 00:35:32,816
It's me.

471
00:35:45,208 --> 00:35:47,134
This is bad.

472
00:36:04,185 --> 00:36:07,355
You look so different,
I didn't even recognize you.

473
00:36:07,355 --> 00:36:09,904
Yeah, I guess.

474
00:36:12,109 --> 00:36:16,915
But why the totally different look?

475
00:36:19,992 --> 00:36:21,682
Well...

476
00:36:23,871 --> 00:36:26,963
You don't have to tell me if you don't want to.

477
00:36:28,422 --> 00:36:30,143
Thank you.

478
00:36:35,495 --> 00:36:37,047
All done.

479
00:36:39,299 --> 00:36:40,946
Just like that?

480
00:36:49,076 --> 00:36:50,732
This is perfect.

481
00:36:52,528 --> 00:36:54,614
You really are a social worker.

482
00:36:55,820 --> 00:36:57,655
I really, really appreciate it.

483
00:36:57,655 --> 00:36:59,782
- Sure.
- I'm so grateful,

484
00:36:59,782 --> 00:37:02,285
but I'm really short on time.

485
00:37:03,955 --> 00:37:06,556
Good karma's coming your way!

486
00:37:06,556 --> 00:37:08,040
Bye!

487
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:11,475
Wait...

488
00:37:14,001 --> 00:37:15,921
What an interesting person.

489
00:37:17,133 --> 00:37:19,045
So if you look here...

490
00:37:19,045 --> 00:37:22,465
Why don't we take a short break?

491
00:37:24,065 --> 00:37:26,443
If you take a look at the...

492
00:37:32,851 --> 00:37:35,500
[Nurimaro Unity Festival]

493
00:38:01,469 --> 00:38:05,348
When is this damn meeting ever going to end?

494
00:38:11,062 --> 00:38:13,827
Hello! We're India Red.

495
00:38:20,988 --> 00:38:23,407
Here's our second song.

496
00:40:27,608 --> 00:40:31,560
<i>Ugh, and I can't even go
to the after-party on a day like this.</i>

497
00:40:33,564 --> 00:40:35,313
<i>That guy...</i>

498
00:40:35,313 --> 00:40:37,482
<i>is he really a social worker?</i>

499
00:40:45,716 --> 00:40:48,427
<i>Not slacking off, I hope.</i>

500
00:40:48,427 --> 00:40:51,013
<i>He's a mind reader.</i>

501
00:40:51,013 --> 00:40:52,882
<i>As if that would scare me.</i>

502
00:40:55,565 --> 00:40:58,272
<i>I'm working myself to pieces.</i>

503
00:41:01,242 --> 00:41:03,746
<i>Worked yourself into dust, then?</i>

504
00:41:03,746 --> 00:41:06,487
<i>Is that why I can't see you anywhere?</i>

505
00:41:06,487 --> 00:41:08,906
<i>No way, is he back already?</i>

506
00:41:09,907 --> 00:41:12,480
<i>He said he'd be back at 8:30!</i>

507
00:41:19,939 --> 00:41:22,130
<i>I still have three stops left!</i>

508
00:41:25,339 --> 00:41:27,466
<i>Don't panic, Eun Chae.</i>

509
00:41:27,466 --> 00:41:29,311
<i>I have an alibi.</i>

510
00:41:33,222 --> 00:41:35,373
<i>I'll be back after dinner!</i>

511
00:41:38,590 --> 00:41:41,105
<i>I'm having dinner. I'll be back soon.</i>

512
00:41:43,850 --> 00:41:45,851
<i>Eating where?</i>

513
00:41:47,739 --> 00:41:49,864
<i>Oh, forget it.</i>

514
00:41:49,864 --> 00:41:52,950
<i>At least let me ride in peace on the way.</i>

515
00:42:00,791 --> 00:42:02,543
Heading to the office?

516
00:42:02,543 --> 00:42:04,003
Yes.

517
00:42:04,003 --> 00:42:05,782
The chairman summoned me.

518
00:42:07,006 --> 00:42:08,549
Better go report to him.

519
00:42:08,549 --> 00:42:10,885
On how Kwon Do Hyeok did today.

520
00:42:10,885 --> 00:42:12,511
It's sushi.

521
00:42:12,511 --> 00:42:14,805
You barely ate earlier.

522
00:42:14,805 --> 00:42:16,307
No need.

523
00:42:16,307 --> 00:42:19,226
Then please give it to Eun Chae.

524
00:42:19,226 --> 00:42:20,811
I'm sure she'd love it.

525
00:42:20,811 --> 00:42:24,732
Why would I do anything
to make that woman happy?

526
00:42:24,732 --> 00:42:27,193
When you do someone a kindness,

527
00:42:27,193 --> 00:42:29,320
do it the way Santa Claus would.

528
00:42:54,090 --> 00:42:55,689
The bouquet!

529
00:42:55,689 --> 00:42:57,591
I'll just take it.

530
00:43:08,025 --> 00:43:09,927
What the heck!

531
00:43:13,197 --> 00:43:15,451
And he wasn't even here...

532
00:43:16,909 --> 00:43:18,830
Look who's talking!

533
00:43:22,430 --> 00:43:26,085
Looks like you've been playing yourself
to pieces.

534
00:43:28,504 --> 00:43:31,090
I left a note.

535
00:43:31,090 --> 00:43:33,509
Saying I'd be back after dinner.

536
00:43:43,159 --> 00:43:44,520
What did you eat?

537
00:43:44,520 --> 00:43:48,107
Do I have to report that, too?

538
00:43:48,107 --> 00:43:51,068
Where did those flowers come from?

539
00:43:53,112 --> 00:43:55,592
I found them on the ground.

540
00:44:05,916 --> 00:44:08,002
What are you doing?

541
00:44:08,002 --> 00:44:09,795
Why would you throw out

542
00:44:09,795 --> 00:44:11,839
someone else's bouquet like that!

543
00:44:11,839 --> 00:44:14,717
You brought trash into my office.

544
00:44:14,717 --> 00:44:17,261
They're pretty, so how is that trash?

545
00:44:17,261 --> 00:44:20,592
Didn't you just say
you found them on the ground?

546
00:44:20,592 --> 00:44:22,141
Exactly!

547
00:44:22,141 --> 00:44:25,530
Some man suddenly tossed them to me,

548
00:44:25,530 --> 00:44:27,125
and I picked them up, that's all.

549
00:44:27,125 --> 00:44:32,443
So, some man
threw flowers at you while you were eating?

550
00:44:32,443 --> 00:44:34,219
I know, right?

551
00:44:48,452 --> 00:44:51,795
I won't have trash like that in my office.

552
00:44:51,795 --> 00:44:54,298
- Throw it out.
- This is my desk.

553
00:44:54,298 --> 00:44:56,300
That desk is company property!

554
00:44:56,300 --> 00:44:57,977
How petty!

555
00:44:59,345 --> 00:45:01,180
Don't you dare touch it.

556
00:45:01,180 --> 00:45:03,932
Touching other people's things is...

557
00:45:03,932 --> 00:45:05,406
What's the crime called?

558
00:45:05,406 --> 00:45:07,071
What is it called!

559
00:45:07,071 --> 00:45:08,103
What?

560
00:45:08,103 --> 00:45:10,189
Misappropriation of lost property?

561
00:45:10,189 --> 00:45:12,024
Right. That one!

562
00:45:12,024 --> 00:45:13,609
That's it!

563
00:45:13,609 --> 00:45:14,610
Enough.

564
00:45:14,610 --> 00:45:17,353
Did you finish everything I told you to do?

565
00:45:21,617 --> 00:45:23,786
Guess not.

566
00:45:23,786 --> 00:45:24,912
Then get to it.

567
00:45:24,912 --> 00:45:27,039
I'm going to eat,

568
00:45:27,039 --> 00:45:29,792
and since you already ate,

569
00:45:29,792 --> 00:45:31,411
you're good, right?

570
00:45:33,959 --> 00:45:36,086
I don't care, whatever.

571
00:46:00,301 --> 00:46:01,833
Is that...

572
00:46:01,833 --> 00:46:03,450
sushi?

573
00:46:03,450 --> 00:46:05,285
It's sushi.

574
00:46:07,204 --> 00:46:10,791
It's a lot for one person, though.

575
00:46:17,005 --> 00:46:19,600
But you did say you'd eaten.

576
00:46:26,056 --> 00:46:28,002
The fish is fresh.

577
00:46:49,913 --> 00:46:52,689
So, sushi...

578
00:46:53,375 --> 00:46:54,461
do you like it?

579
00:46:54,461 --> 00:46:57,158
<i>If you don't, pass it to me.</i>

580
00:46:59,167 --> 00:47:00,787
It's just food.

581
00:47:02,342 --> 00:47:04,344
<i>Just food?</i>

582
00:47:04,344 --> 00:47:07,710
<i>If sushi's "just food" to you, hand it over.</i>

583
00:47:12,140 --> 00:47:15,185
I do like sushi, though...

584
00:47:16,336 --> 00:47:17,788
I didn't ask.

585
00:47:19,606 --> 00:47:22,540
Then what food do you like?

586
00:47:23,530 --> 00:47:25,603
I've never thought about that.

587
00:47:26,598 --> 00:47:29,434
Clean this up for me.

588
00:47:43,008 --> 00:47:44,698
Shall I...

589
00:47:44,698 --> 00:47:47,025
clean it up?

590
00:47:53,674 --> 00:47:55,126
Oh, my.

591
00:47:56,063 --> 00:47:59,650
It's tuna and flounder belly!

592
00:48:02,783 --> 00:48:03,820
I can't help it.

593
00:48:03,820 --> 00:48:05,587
I'm hungry.

594
00:48:15,796 --> 00:48:17,367
It's so good.

595
00:48:23,270 --> 00:48:25,970
Didn't you say you'd eaten dinner?

596
00:48:26,637 --> 00:48:29,930
If you leave food,
you have to eat it all in heaven.

597
00:48:29,930 --> 00:48:33,809
So I forced myself to eat it
even though I'm full.

598
00:48:35,090 --> 00:48:36,853
Good job.

599
00:48:36,853 --> 00:48:38,388
Well done.

600
00:48:39,147 --> 00:48:40,912
Heaven sounds nice.

601
00:48:49,897 --> 00:48:51,883
Whatever.

602
00:49:01,542 --> 00:49:03,720
It's already past 11.

603
00:49:07,410 --> 00:49:09,177
This guy won't even go home.

604
00:49:09,177 --> 00:49:10,429
What is he doing?

605
00:49:39,041 --> 00:49:43,170
<i>When the CEO is in the lab,
never, ever disturb him.</i>

606
00:49:43,851 --> 00:49:46,070
What is he doing in there?

607
00:49:48,133 --> 00:49:50,207
That sex addict.

608
00:49:51,053 --> 00:49:53,047
Is he watching something dirty?

609
00:50:25,061 --> 00:50:27,964
<i>Why is it so firm?</i>

610
00:50:31,927 --> 00:50:34,910
<i>Why is my heart pounding?</i>

611
00:50:42,062 --> 00:50:43,313
What's this?

612
00:50:43,313 --> 00:50:47,192
What on earth is this room, anyway?

613
00:50:47,192 --> 00:50:48,985
You even locked the door.

614
00:50:48,985 --> 00:50:52,516
There are things we shouldn't watch together.

615
00:50:52,516 --> 00:50:55,392
Then please finish what you were doing.

616
00:50:55,392 --> 00:50:57,828
I'm going home now.

617
00:50:57,828 --> 00:51:00,391
I have a midnight curfew.

618
00:51:00,391 --> 00:51:01,623
Curfew?

619
00:51:01,623 --> 00:51:04,084
Your lies come in all varieties.

620
00:51:04,084 --> 00:51:05,377
No, it's not a lie.

621
00:51:09,798 --> 00:51:11,473
Look.

622
00:51:15,429 --> 00:51:19,307
Dad, I'm really still at work.

623
00:51:19,307 --> 00:51:21,101
Dad.

624
00:51:21,101 --> 00:51:23,353
What an elaborate plan.

625
00:51:23,353 --> 00:51:24,563
Impressive.

626
00:51:29,025 --> 00:51:32,529
Dad, I'll put someone on
to prove I'm really at work.

627
00:51:32,529 --> 00:51:35,574
This is Manager Kwon.

628
00:51:36,093 --> 00:51:37,642
Impressive.

629
00:51:39,083 --> 00:51:42,581
<i>Oh my, Manager Kwon, is it?</i>

630
00:51:42,581 --> 00:51:47,085
Yes, I'm Eun Chae's father.

631
00:51:49,838 --> 00:51:51,757
Yes...

632
00:51:51,757 --> 00:51:54,345
Taeyun Group marketing!

633
00:51:54,345 --> 00:51:57,345
You must be so busy,

634
00:51:57,345 --> 00:51:59,181
<i>but...</i>

635
00:51:59,181 --> 00:52:04,478
<i>it's not like we only live for today.</i>

636
00:52:04,478 --> 00:52:10,066
<i>Your company must have rules
that employees have to follow.</i>

637
00:52:10,066 --> 00:52:14,839
I also have something I want
my child to follow,

638
00:52:14,839 --> 00:52:17,491
and that's a curfew.

639
00:52:17,491 --> 00:52:18,492
Yes.

640
00:52:18,492 --> 00:52:21,046
As it happens, we were about to leave now.

641
00:52:21,046 --> 00:52:24,664
As you know, it's a rough world out there.

642
00:52:24,664 --> 00:52:26,644
I'm sure you understand.

643
00:52:26,644 --> 00:52:27,793
Yes.

644
00:52:27,793 --> 00:52:32,589
I'll see your daughter home on my way.

645
00:52:35,796 --> 00:52:38,924
That's new from you.

646
00:52:40,222 --> 00:52:41,848
No need.

647
00:52:41,848 --> 00:52:43,661
I can go home by myself.

648
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:45,644
I made a promise to your father.

649
00:52:45,644 --> 00:52:48,435
If I don't keep it, that makes me a liar.

650
00:52:48,435 --> 00:52:50,980
I can't stand that.

651
00:52:56,511 --> 00:53:00,002
What happens if you miss your curfew?

652
00:53:00,002 --> 00:53:01,618
My head gets shaved.

653
00:53:01,618 --> 00:53:02,786
Oh, come on.

654
00:53:02,786 --> 00:53:05,372
Right? Everyone says that.

655
00:53:05,372 --> 00:53:07,666
That's because they don't know my father.

656
00:53:07,666 --> 00:53:09,543
With such a scary father,

657
00:53:09,543 --> 00:53:12,195
why lie about working at Taeyun Group?

658
00:53:12,195 --> 00:53:14,788
That was a white lie.

659
00:53:15,536 --> 00:53:17,968
Never told one, have you?

660
00:53:17,968 --> 00:53:20,512
It just turned out that way.

661
00:53:20,512 --> 00:53:23,951
But with a company like ours,
couldn't you just be honest?

662
00:53:23,951 --> 00:53:25,642
Forget it.

663
00:53:25,642 --> 00:53:28,228
Who knows what happens after three months.

664
00:53:28,228 --> 00:53:32,357
Maybe once I'm a real full-timer
at a big company.

665
00:53:32,357 --> 00:53:36,361
Are big companies and full-time
jobs that important?

666
00:53:36,361 --> 00:53:40,991
Someone like you,
who was born on third base, wouldn't know.

667
00:53:40,991 --> 00:53:45,365
For us to even reach first, we have to bunt.

668
00:53:55,133 --> 00:53:57,940
The light's still on.

669
00:53:57,940 --> 00:53:59,301
Your father?

670
00:53:59,301 --> 00:54:01,636
Yes, go before we get caught...

671
00:54:06,600 --> 00:54:09,320
- What's going on?
- My father's right there!

672
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:30,674
Coast is clear.

673
00:54:41,217 --> 00:54:43,930
What, what's wrong?

674
00:54:43,930 --> 00:54:45,805
A cramp... a cramp...

675
00:54:45,805 --> 00:54:47,140
I have a cramp.

676
00:54:47,140 --> 00:54:48,558
Yeah, a cramp, okay.

677
00:54:48,558 --> 00:54:50,143
Hand, hand! Let go,

678
00:54:50,143 --> 00:54:51,811
let go of my hand!

679
00:54:51,811 --> 00:54:53,504
Sorry!

680
00:54:55,346 --> 00:54:57,848
Hand, hand, hand!

681
00:55:03,337 --> 00:55:05,424
Ouch, ouch!

682
00:55:12,457 --> 00:55:14,417
What are you doing?

683
00:55:14,417 --> 00:55:16,211
You said you had a cramp!

684
00:55:16,211 --> 00:55:17,253
Stop it!

685
00:55:17,253 --> 00:55:18,838
Just hold still!

686
00:55:18,838 --> 00:55:20,532
I'm trying to help.

687
00:55:36,603 --> 00:55:41,998
<i>I'm just letting him hold my foot for a moment.</i>

688
00:55:42,821 --> 00:55:46,250
<i>I'm only doing this in case she can't walk.</i>

689
00:55:58,992 --> 00:56:01,685
<i>What's with the mood all of a sudden?</i>

690
00:56:02,429 --> 00:56:04,278
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

691
00:56:52,640 --> 00:56:54,142
<i>- Oh, my!
- First time?</i>

692
00:56:54,142 --> 00:56:54,851
<i>No?</i>

693
00:56:54,851 --> 00:56:57,251
<i>I've had about a truckload.</i>

694
00:56:57,251 --> 00:56:59,773
<i>Nervous? Not like you, Lee Eun Chae.</i>

695
00:56:59,773 --> 00:57:02,275
<i>Guess all you have is a sex drive.</i>

696
00:57:02,275 --> 00:57:04,486
<i>It's my first time showing.</i>

697
00:57:04,486 --> 00:57:06,780
<i>You do have people you're close to, right?</i>

698
00:57:06,780 --> 00:57:07,864
<i>You.</i>

699
00:57:07,864 --> 00:57:10,283
<i>Think I'd fall for this?</i>

700
00:57:10,283 --> 00:57:13,536
<i>If that's acting, it deserves an award.</i>

701
00:57:13,536 --> 00:57:15,789
<i>He is good-looking, though.</i>

702
00:57:15,789 --> 00:57:17,582
<i>Don't mind what others think.</i>

703
00:57:17,582 --> 00:57:19,186
<i>You'll need the power of love.</i>
